{"name":"Lavender Blue Shadow","hex":"#8b88f8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lavender","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of European plants, genus, Lavandula, of the mint family.","A pale bluish purple or violet colour, like that of the lavender flower."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale purple colour.","Pertaining to LGBT people and rights."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lavender"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"shadow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark image projected onto a surface where light (or other radiation) is blocked by the shade of an object.","Relative darkness, especially as caused by the interruption of light; gloom; obscurity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unofficial, informal, unauthorized, but acting as though it were.","Having power or influence, but not widely known or recognized."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shadow of the Ninja","blocks":[{"text":"Shadow of the Ninja, originally released in Japan as Yami no Shigotonin Kage  and later released in Europe and Australia as Blue Shadow, is a 1990 hack and slash platform game developed and published by Natsume for the Nintendo Entertainment System. The game revolves around a pair of ninja sent to assassinate a dictator in a futuristic version of New York City. A port was planned for the Game Boy, but was released in a rebranded form as Ninja Gaiden Shadow. A remake, Shadow of the Ninja: Reborn, was released in 2024."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/99/Shadow_of_the_Ninja_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow_of_the_Ninja","wikidata":"Q2498075"},{"title":"Lavender's Blue","blocks":[{"text":"\"Lavender's Blue\" is an English folk song and nursery rhyme from the 17th century. Its Roud Folk Song Index number is 3483. It has been recorded in various forms and some pop versions have been hits in the U.S. and U.K. charts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Diddle%2C_diddle._Or%2C_The_kind_country_lovers_%28bod23683%29.png/330px-Diddle%2C_diddle._Or%2C_The_kind_country_lovers_%28bod23683%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavender's_Blue","wikidata":"Q3445529"},{"title":"Periwinkle (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Periwinkle is a color in the blue and violet family. Its name is derived from the lesser periwinkle or myrtle herb which bears flowers of the same color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Vinca_minor_Nashville.jpg/330px-Vinca_minor_Nashville.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Periwinkle_(color)","wikidata":"Q2617229"},{"title":"Lavandula","blocks":[{"text":"Lavandula is a genus of 47 known species of perennial flowering plants in the sage family, Lamiaceae. It is native to regions of the Iberian Peninsula and Mediterranean coastline, the Middle East, extending to the Indian subcontinent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Single_lavender_flower02.jpg/330px-Single_lavender_flower02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lavandula","wikidata":"Q171892"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b7/NesShad